rtup packet; statuses remain provisional. Overflow records are explicit and require their source pointers.","readiness":{"blockers":"NO_OFFICIAL_SOURCE_LOCATED|ONLY_COMPILED_TRANSCRIPTION_FOUND|NO_CLAUSE_INVENTORY|FIRST_END_UNPROVED|SAVINGS_RESIDUALS_NOT_CLOSED","claim_present":"no","claim_record_errors":"","decision_origin":"inherited_legacy_v2","exhausted_steps":"","factual_event_policy_errors":"","instrument_id":"EO:8747","opus_media_applicability_note":"","original_copy_replacement_required":"no","provisional_status":"no","quotation_recheck_required":"no","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"done","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"n/a","step_original_text":"open","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"6","steps_done":"2","text_evidence_tier":"missing","working_text_policy_errors":""},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"original_text","what":"no official original-text candidate from any job; fr-originals: ofr_index_not_received_for_publication (The OFR index marks this order 'not received for publication', so it was probably never printed in the Federal Register (OFR catalog statement, not verified here). Other routes: NARA, presidential lib); 1 compiled-transcription lead(s) (for example Richardson) point to the text but are not the original by themselves"},{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Whereas, in my judgment, the public interest requires that Louis A. Simon, Supervising Architect of the Public Buildings Administration, Federal Works Agency, who was exempted from compulsory retirement for age for periods totaling four years by Executive Orders No. 7581 of March 19, 1937, No. 7824 of February 25, 1938, No. 8046 of February 11, 1939, and No. 8369 of March 7, 1940, be further exempted from such compulsory retirement for a period of six months:\n\nNow, Therefore, by virtue of and pursuant to the authority vested in me by section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), I hereby further exempt the said Louis A. Simon from compulsory retirement for age for a period of six months ending November 30, 1941.\n\nFRANKLIN D ROOSEVELT\n\nThe White House,\n\nApril 28, 1941.\n","path":"jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-8747-exemption-louis-simon-from-compulsory-retirement-for-age.txt","sha256":"326a6ee892d8e1aee379874e75fe93786ff21c9e349bc0cd32bd5b7baf099889","source":{"line":8635,"path":"jobs/app-transcriptions/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"bb9d39be0d0e5f316938b18d8a8d6a19e15a126f4ed554a6fc89adabcb911d06"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 8747—Exemption of Louis A. Simon From Compulsory Retirement for Age\n\nWhereas, in my judgment, the public interest requires that Louis A. Simon, Supervising Architect of the Public Buildings Administration, Federal Works Agency, who was exempted from compulsory retirement for age for periods totaling four years by Executive Orders No. 7581 of March 19, 1937, No. 7824 of February 25, 1938, No. 8046 of February 11, 1939, and No. 8369 of March 7, 1940, be further exempted from such compulsory retirement for a period of six months:\n\nNow, Therefore, by virtue of and pursuant to the authority vested in me by section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), I hereby further exempt the said Louis A. Simon from compulsory retirement for age for a period of six months ending November 30, 1941.\n\nFRANKLIN D ROOSEVELT\n\nThe White House,\n\nApril 28, 1941.","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-app-executive-orders-8747-f60c5e643e.txt","sha256":"b9426bb8d91159a77ba316351d6d23043d4ab7b626081f4474d8d397c2a051bb","source":{"line":4161,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"a4ded2adc00aabcfe9fe5e1f20bec1c1598c302501f0e0a09959b473b190c752"}}]}
